{
  "core_message": "A 1898 novella eerily predicted the Titanic disaster fourteen years later.",
  "mood": "curious",
  "title": "13 survivors from an 1898 ship that predicted Titanic",
  "description": "Morgan Robertson’s novel *Futility* described a fictional liner, the Titan, that sank after striking an iceberg in 1898. Fourteen years later, the real Titanic met the same fate, sparking speculation of prophetic foresight.\n\nKey points:\n• 1898 novel warned of an iceberg collision and insufficient lifeboats.\n• Only thirteen survivors were reported.\n• The book was reissued after Titanic’s wreck, highlighting uncanny parallels.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"The Wreck of the Titan: Or, Futility\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wreck_of_the_Titan:_Or,_Futility), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\nImage credits:\nTitan-crystal bar.JPG (Alchemist-hp ( pse-mendelejew.de ), CC BY-SA 3.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Titan-crystal_bar.JPG\nVince Zampella.jpg (Dean Takahashi, CC BY-SA 4.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vince_Zampella.jpg\nTitan Missile Family.png (Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Titan_Missile_Family.png\nWreck and sinking of the Titanic - the ocean's greatest disaster - a graphic and thrilling account of the sinking of the greatest floating palace ever built, carrying down to watery graves more than (14593187138).jpg (Internet Archive Book Images, No restrictions): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wreck_and_sinking_of_the_Titanic_-_the_ocean%27s_greatest_disaster_-_a_graphic_and_thrilling_account_of_the_sinking_of_the_greatest_floating_palace_ever_built,_carrying_down_to_watery_graves_more_than_(14593187138).jpg\n\n3D models:\nIce Block by bilgehan.korkmaz (CC BY 4.0) https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/none-66efdeab7d214907b32bbcb47d9b55ad\nPolar Bear by cedes (CC BY-SA 4.0) https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/none-401e5a7e5ad04f498cbfe1b7054d83ec",
